  "title": "About Us",
  "content": "SCIENCE CHINA is a comprehensive academic journal jointly sponsored by the Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS) and the National Natural Science Foundation of China. Founded in 1950, SCIENCE CHINA has developed into a domestic top-level scientific journal in terms of academic level, editing quality and publishing quality.\n                \n              \n              \n                \n                Chinese Science Bulletin is a multidisciplinary academic journal supervised by the Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS) and co-sponsored by CAS and the National Natural Science Foundation of China.\nChinese Science Bulletin publishes high-caliber, peer-reviewed research on topics across the natural sciences and various high-tech fields from global science community. Journal articles are selected on the basis of originality, scientific significance and appeal to a general audience.\n              The Tan Kah Kee Science Awards grew out of the former Tan Kah Kee Awards, which were established in 1988 in honor of Mr. Tan Kah Kee (1874–1961), a well-known overseas Chinese leader who made remarkable contributions to the development of science and education in China. The Tan Kah Kee Awards were first established by Mr. Tan’s relatives. Later, CAS was entrusted for its organization and evaluation.",
